# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Revenue Guardian — frontend environment
#
# Copy to .env for local development. For a Vercel deployment, set these in the
# frontend project's Environment Variables.
#
# Only VITE_* variables reach the browser, and everything here is public by
# construction. No provider secret belongs in this file: not
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET, not RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, not POLLINATIONS_API_KEY,
# not WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN, not SMTP_PASSWORD. Those live only in the backend
# project, and the browser never talks to WhatsApp or SMTP directly.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Backend API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the dashboard sends every request. No trailing slash.
#
# This is read at BUILD time, not at runtime: changing it in Vercel requires a
# redeploy to take effect. A production build made without it points at
# http://localhost:3000 and fails on the visitor's machine — the app says so
# explicitly in the console and in its error messages rather than looking broken.
#
# Local:  http://localhost:3000
# Vercel: https://your-backend-project.vercel.app
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Supabase (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dashboard has no sign-in and reads nothing from Supabase directly — the
# database is reached through the backend's Prisma client. These exist only
# because a Supabase auth attacher is registered for server functions; the app
# currently defines none, so the client is never constructed.
#
# Set them if you add server functions that need a Supabase session. The
# publishable key is safe to expose; a service-role key never is.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=

# ── Build ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Selects the Nitro build target. `vercel.json` already sets this for Vercel
# builds; you only need it if you build for Vercel by hand.
# NITRO_PRESET=vercel
